  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Port native ordinary 3D rigid-joint construction, limits, motors, orthogonalization and colored impulse solving in mirrored Rust module paths.",
  "regressions": [
    "Thirty-six live native cases cover empty/partial/strided lanes, interleaved batches, twelve joint configurations, biased/unbiased solve, zero timestep, offset COM, anisotropic inertia and both motor models.",
    "Strict guards, IDs, impulse bounds and all endpoint write conflicts, including static and zero-row joints, are checked independently of numeric tolerance.",
    "Metal angular motors exercise asin lowering and C tail cases reject missing dispatch guards."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Shared row construction is factored behind named Rust method counterparts in joint_constraint_builder.py; ABI offsets come only from Rust.",
    "The pinned compiler needs target-specific Metal asin intrinsic registration; the native equation and precision remain unchanged.",
    "Explicit outer lane guards avoid constant strided-loop tail elimination by the pinned compiler.",
    "Native coupled angular omissions and maximum-only coupled linear limits are preserved and recorded as reference limitations.",
    "Rigid-joint scene integration and runtime color construction remain separate work. Ascend is source lowering only."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0037-connected-analytic-scenes"
  ]
}
